      ],
      "text": "Cost 1 Mythic Point\n\n---\nEffect Belimarius regains an expended spell."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Sacrifice Warshard",
      "actions": "free",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "divine",
        "emotion",
        "incapacitation",
        "manipulate",
        "mental"
      ],
      "text": "Trigger Belimarius begins her turn\n\nRequirements Belimarius has the warshard of Gorum held in a hand\n\n---\nEffect While its mythic potential and divine power has largely been used to transform the Eye of Desire and the Runewell of Lust into the forms described in Chapter 1 to enable her imminent mythic ascension, enough power remains within to generate one final effect. With a quick motion, Belimarius crushes the mostly depleted warshard she holds in her hand, destroying it and causing red rain to cascade down around her in a 120-foot emanation (which easily fills the entirety of the Eye of Desire). Allies in this area (Belimarius and her two knights of malice) become Quickened for 1 minute but can use the extra action only to Strike with a melee weapon. Foes in the area (including the PCs) must attempt a DC 41 Will save save.\n\n---\nCritical Success The creature absorbs some of Gorum's legacy and gains 1 Mythic Point that they must spend before the end of their next turn.\n\nSuccess The creature is unaffected.\n\nFailure The creature is overwhelmed with despair at Gorum's death and becomes Stunned 1.\n\nCritical Failure The creature becomes Paralyzed with despair at Gorum's death. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can attempt a DC 41 Will save save to end the effect, with the DC lowered by 2 each subsequent round."
